# Website Tracker Implementation Guide

## 📌 Overview

This document provides a **step-by-step, production-ready implementation guide** for the website tracker system. The tracker captures:
- **Bot Identification** (AI crawlers, search engines, etc.)
- **AI Crawler Behavior & Activity** (crawl patterns, content accessed, frequency)
- **Human Visitor Demographics** (device, OS, browser, location)
- **Traffic Sources** (referrer, UTM parameters, classification)
- **Geographic & Location Data** (country, city, timezone, ISP)

The tracker operates in **two layers**:
1. **Client-side**: Lightweight JavaScript tag embedded in user websites (no tracking consent required for crawlers)
2. **Server-side**: Aggregation, analysis, and storage with strict security & performance optimization

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  CLIENT WEBSITE (User's Domain)                         │
│  <script src="tracker.js" data-project-id="..."></script>
│  ↓ Captures Page Visit → Detects Bot/Device/Geo        │
└──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                   │ POST /api/tracking/capture
┌──────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────────┐
│  GEO-TRACKER BACKEND                                    │
│  ├─ No Auth Required (Public API)                       │
│  ├─ Validates project ID                               │
│  ├─ Parses User-Agent → Bot Detection                  │
│  ├─ Geolocation Lookup (IP-based)                       │
│  ├─ Device/Browser Detection                           │
│  └─ Queues Raw Event → Database                        │
└──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────┘
                   │
┌──────────────────▼──────────────────────────────────────┐
│  DATABASE SCHEMA (PostgreSQL)                           │
│                                                          │
│  Raw Events Layer:                                      │
│  ├─ page_visits (raw events, high-volume)              │
│  ├─ bot_detectors (bot patterns & metadata)            │
│                                                          │
│  Aggregated Analytics Layer:                            │
│  ├─ ai_crawler_logs (daily bot summaries)              │
│  ├─ traffic_sources (daily referrer summaries)         │
│  ├─ visitor_demographics (daily device summaries)      │
│  └─ geographic_activity (daily geo summaries)          │
│                                                          │
│  Lookup Tables:                                         │
